DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261202T193000
DTSTAMP:20261127T084111Z
UID:dd82f801dce1b52f21908652c457@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Art + Design\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Join MODA for the final session of our 2026 Business x Design 
 season\, facilitated by Gene Kansas. Alisa Barry grew Bella Cucina from a 
 small Atlanta café into a line of artisan pantry goods sold around the wo
 rld. Smith Hanes founded Smith Hanes Studio\, the design firm behind some 
 of Atlanta’s best-known dining rooms\, including The Optimist and Atrium
  at Ponce City Market. Alisa and Smith will talk about how food\, space\, 
 ritual\, and atmosphere work together to create hospitality\, and how each
  of them turned a personal craft into a values-driven business.\nCategory:
  Art + Design\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/business-x-
 design-alisa-barry-of-bella-cucina-and-smith-hanes-of-smith-hanes-studio/
